build/bin/
frontend/node_modules/
frontend/dist/
*.db
*.db-wal
*.db-shm
dist/
wailsjs/
.DS_Store
# Build artifact: `wails build` generates <Name>-res.syso in the package root and
# deletes it afterwards; build.ps1 and air stage copies of the objects below
# there for the duration of a plain `go build`. None of those are committed.
/*.syso
# ...but the committed per-architecture resource objects are tracked. They stay
# in build/windows so they can never sit next to the one Wails generates: two
# .rsrc sections in a single link fail with "too many .rsrc sections".
!build/windows/*-res_windows_*.syso
# Air's working dir + stray local Go cache.
tmp/
.tmp-go-cache/
